NetHack 3.1 Bugs II:

   1)  A SPOILER mentioned recently which essentially told of a "neat" 
       trick in which one could sell things that were still considered
       unpaid for in a shop by throwing them a certain way is SICK!!
       Please powers that be (i.e. Dev Team) fix this in the next patch!
      
   2)  Bug or feature?  I've always noticed that when one reads a scroll
       of magic mapping on a leprachaun vault level w/o having first dis-
       covered the teleport trap to the vault, that the trap no longer 
       exists.
   
   3)  My friend told me of a weird bug in the gnomish town.  One game in
       which he teleported one of the shopkeepers out of his shop and then
       died.  When another character came back to this level, all of the
       shops were said to be "deserted" by the shopkeepers even though in
       all of them the shopkeepers were standing right at the inside of the
       doors as usual.  Everything went fine in a buggy way with these 
       unmoving "nonexisten" shopkeepers until one of them, under the in-
       fluece of the ring of conflict, attacked an orc in his store.  
       When my friend entered the store of this "reactivated" shopkeeper,
       the game immediately froze! (this game has been recovered to a point
       right before the crash for any intrested parties).

   4)  Evidently a sure way to put the program in disorder while in a shop 
       is to loot a chest and try to pay for the looted item (perhaps only
       after the whole unit is picked up?).  At least according to a firend
       of mine.
    
   5)  Can Liches blind you?  If so, and it wasn't some stupid mistake on
       my part with a blindfold, I believe I recieved some incurable blind-
       ness.  My uncursed unicorn's horn wouldn't help me nor did it list 
       me as being blind in the final listing of intrinsics.  What?

   6)  Arrgh!  Maybe it's just me but I feel self-polymorphing needs a 
       little restructuring!  The idea that one can just pretty much stay
       a vampire lord with an automatic bonus of 10 to their AC plus a
       host of other nifties only return their old undamaged selves if
       anything managages to hit and kill one's -30 AC or more entity.
       My complaint is twofold: 1. If one polymorphs into a more powerful
       (i.e. higher HD) creature and gets killed, one should definitely
       at least take some of the damage to the original self!  2. When
       morphing into another humanoid I don't think there should always
       be an automatic adding of AC's.  How much of a dwarf's AC is from
       their speed, size, and toughness vs. actual armor worn?  The part of
       a humanoid's AC that falls under actual armor shouldn't be added to
       the morphed character.  One can't wear two dwarvish sets of body
       armor at the same time can they?  If so I feel godlike, untouchable
       AC is much too easy to obtain.

   7)  Finally, I'd like to thank Mike Marcelais and the Fourth Bryan
       Productions team for Chrhack.  Included with this or posted in
       close proximity is the work of Robert M. Wagner (a.k.a. Paladin)
       and myself, Tim F. Jordan (Lord Gek) in creating a complete graph-
       ical rendering of all the monsters and a little reworking of 
       some of the basic rooms/objects symbols.  I hear there is a 
       ChrHack2.1 that possibly among other things, fixes the "Rogue"
       level stuff.  I hope this, having been made on the 2.0 version is
       still compatible (if not hopefully someone would be kind enough to
       convert it).


